 ## Unreleased
 
+- Tax uses the rates in force on the invoice's issue date, which is now required.
+  Germany's reduced rate (food, books) is 9% from 2027-01-01.
 - Fixed: UK food and books were charged 20% VAT; both are zero-rated.
 - Quantities may be fractional, down to 0.01 with at most two decimal places (hours of services, say).
   Printed invoices and exported records show them as decimals.
